   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the public officers law, in relation to the filing of\nfinancial disclosure statements",
    "basePrintNo": "S6184",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S6184-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §73-a, Pub Off L",
    "lawSection": "Public Officers Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S6184\n\nSPONSOR: SKOUFIS\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the public officers law, in relation to the filing of\nfinancial disclosure statements\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nEnsures parity between grade 24 employees of CSEA and PEF as both being\nexempt from the requirement to file a Financial Disclosure Statement\n(FDS) with the NYS Commission on Ethics and Lobbying in Government.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1: Uses the job rate for salary grade (SG) 24 public employees\nfor CSEA or PEF members, whichever is higher, as the threshold for\nfiling a Financial Disclosure Statement.\n\nSection 2: Establishes the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nCurrent law uses the CSEA salary grade 24 job rate as the income limit\nfor being exempt from filing a Financial Disclosure Statement with the\nNYS Commission on Ethics and Lobbying in Government. If both CSEA and\nPEF members have current contracts, this amount is the same for members\nof both unions. However, recently the CSEA contract expired, meaning\nthat the salary for all their members, including SG 24, did not\nincrease. At the same time, the PEF contract was in effect and provided\nwage increases to its members on April 1, meaning that PEF grade 24\nmembers' salary was temporarily higher than that of their CSEA counter-\nparts. This temporarily higher salary triggered the requirement for them\nto fill out the disclosure statement.\n\nThis legislation would use the higher of the CSEA or PEF SG 24 job rate\nsalaries as the income limit. This would mean that certain PEF members,\nwhen the CSEA contract has expired, would no longer have to complete the\nform for one year or seek an exemption from filing.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nSenate\n\nNew bill.\n\nAssembly\n\n2023-2024: A5308, Referred to government operations\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on the first of April next succeeding the\ndate on which it shall have become a law.\n",
